{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"agent_message","text":"## Verified closures\n\n- **R2 finding 2 — closed:** MapEntry payload `[:a 1]` now round-trips correctly and receives the same address as the equivalent vector.\n- **R2 finding 5 — closed:** A correctly hashed lambda row with metadata on its params vector now throws `:slot-kind`.\n\nIndependently confirmed **19 tests / 157 assertions / 0 failures**.\n\n## Remaining and new findings\n\n### 1. Blocking | [v2.cljc:647](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:647) | Nested metadata corruption is reachable through the real frontend\n\nI reproduced silent corruption using ordinary reader syntax passed through `yang/compile`:\n\n```clojure\n(if true\n  ^{:note ^{:meaning 1} x} []\n  ^{:note ^{:meaning 2} x} [])\n```\n\nBefore conversion, the nested symbols carry `{:meaning 1}` and `{:meaning 2}`. After reconstruction, **both carry `{:meaning 2}`**.\n\nThe claim that no real frontend produces this shape is therefore false. This shares the encoder’s scalar-metadata limitation, but it requires neither pathological symbol construction nor a custom collection. The projection can prevent silent corruption without fixing the encoder.\n\n**Recommended fix:** Recursively compare metadata itself, or explicitly reject unsupported nested metadata before sharing. A docstring exclusion alone does not prevent the demonstrated corruption.\n\n### 2. Blocking | [v2.cljc:630](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:630) | Normal reader-generated provenance survives stripping\n\nThe original `{:note (with-meta 'x {:line 77})}` reproduction remains reachable.\n\nMore significantly, reading this source with Clojure’s `LineNumberingPushbackReader`:\n\n```clojure\n^{:note (helper x)} []\n```\n\nautomatically attaches `{:line 1 :column 9}` to the metadata’s list value. Passing it through `yang/compile` and both conversion functions preserves those positions.\n\nThis is ordinary reader output, not merely a manually constructed metadata-on-metadata object. It remains a payload-exclusion defect even where addresses are unaffected.\n\n**Recommended fix:** Recursively strip reader positions from retained metadata, including its nested values and its own metadata. Keep semantic metadata intact.\n\n### 3. Blocking — new | [v2.cljc:732](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:732) | Operand-vector metadata has the same asymmetry just fixed for params\n\nA correctly hashed application body containing:\n\n```clojure\n[:application operator-id (with-meta [] {:purpose 1}) false]\n```\n\npasses reconstruction. The `:nodes` branch rebuilds operands with `mapv`, discarding their metadata. Re-projection therefore produces a different address. I reproduced `rows → map → rows` returning unequal results.\n\nThis also applies to `:dao.stream.apply/call` operands.\n\n**Recommended fix:** Require metadata-free `:nodes` vectors during reconstruction, consistently with the new `:syms` check. Test both tags.\n\n### 4. Non-blocking, explicitly deferred | [v2.cljc:652](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:652) | Custom-comparator set matching remains limited\n\nThe comparator-defined set counterexample remains unsupported. Unlike nested metadata, it requires deliberately constructing a set whose comparator distinguishes `=`-equal elements. Deferring this case is defensible for this unit, provided the restricted collection semantics remain explicit; it cannot support an unrestricted claim of correctness over every collection admitted by `plain-data?`.\n\n**Recommended follow-up:** Enforce that restriction at validation, or implement one-to-one metadata-sensitive element matching.\n\n## Verdict\n\n**No — not ready for Architect sign-off.**\n\nBefore sign-off:\n\n1. Prevent silent nested-metadata merging.\n2. Strip reader provenance recursively through metadata.\n3. Reject metadata-bearing child-ID vectors before reconstruction changes them.\n\nThe custom-comparator set limitation can be disclosed and deferred. The broader validator omissions remain separate outstanding work; this review does not mark them implemented.\n\nNo files were edited. Verification was JVM-only."}}
